From be6b75e013161b6dae22202625cd39b1ad2243e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Intel MPSS <mpss@intel.invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 10:50:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] opcodes: KNC disassembler

From Intel MPSS 3.8.6: decode the MVEX 0x62 map with swizzles,
conversions, broadcasts, {eh}, rounding/SAE and compressed disp8, the
KNC mask and scalar VEX instructions, and jknzd/jkzd.

Only done for bfd_mach_k1om: 0x62 in 64-bit mode stays invalid
elsewhere, and the KNC VEX instructions are looked up in their own
table ahead of vex_table instead of occupying vex_table slots.  All
KNC tables live in i386-dis-mvex.h.  Intel's L1OM decoder (the D6 map
and the L1OM half of the 62 map) is left out.

The bfd, opcodes and include parts of binutils knc-2.45 d12b623d816.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
---
